  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nArea of low pressure will continue to dive south of the area with \ndrier and cooler weather taking hold, with surface high pressure \nbuilding in from the north. Areas of fog will be possible overnight, \nparticularly in sheltered valleys, along with patchy frost expected \nacross the northern mountains in sheltered valleys. In coordination \nwith other offices, elected to issue a frost advisory for the \nhighest elevations of the northern mountains. This is mainly a\nconcern in sheltered valleys as winds should be enough on ridge\ntops to prevent much in the way of formation.\n\nThe area should remain dry, cool, and mostly sunny, although a few \nclouds may appear from time to time particularly across the east as \nlow pressure slowly rides north along the coast through the\nweekend. Gradually warmer conditions take hold to start next \nweek as weak ridging builds in ahead of the next approaching \nsystem, progged to affect the area by mid week.",
